<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4676] Closure hangs if executed nested internal task with continuation</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4676</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Initially this bug found in following scenario.&lt;br/&gt;
Client send task T1 to node B via node A.&lt;br/&gt;
Node A sends closure ExeCallable to node B and add listener to taskFuture.&lt;br/&gt;
On node B ExeCallable executed internal task with one job with continuation.&lt;br/&gt;
Result of ExeCallable never returned to node A.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The problem isolated in GridJobWorker &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;final&lt;/span&gt; ThreadLocal&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Boolean&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; HOLD&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; variable does not change its state in valid way for internal tasks and never call &lt;tt&gt;finishJob()&lt;/tt&gt; method.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
